    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d901">

                <pb facs="1151" n="1049" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg1049"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867.248 Martin Co., Glenn L./18: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Skinner</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ankara</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-02-21T12:00:00+02:00">February 21,
                            1935—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 1:40 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5. Prime Minister requests me to state Turkish Government has arranged to buy 16
                    Martin bombers in the United States. Manufacturers are producing four bombers
                    monthly but on account of War Department orders cannot undertake to deliver more
                    than one monthly to Turkey beginning next year. Prime Minister expresses urgent
                    hope that American Government will authorize manufacturers to deliver two
                    bombers monthly to Turkey beginning in August. Knowing as I do that Turkish
                    Government extremely anxious to obtain these deliveries I trust Department may
                    be able to obtain prompt and favorable decision.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Skinner</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
